infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Pushing data to the client: HTTP vs WebSocket
  desc Why the server cannot afford to push over plain HTTP
  compares
    - label HTTP request-response
      children
        - label Round-trips per server push
          desc 1 full RTT every single delivery
        - label Who can initiate
          desc Client only — server must wait to be asked
        - label Connection
          desc New request each time; no persistent push channel
        - label Live-data fit
          desc Structurally wrong — latency stacks per message
    - label WebSocket
      children
        - label Round-trips per server push
          desc 0 after the one-time upgrade
        - label Who can initiate
          desc Either side, at any moment (full-duplex)
        - label Connection
          desc One persistent socket reused; 0 extra TCP/TLS
        - label Message latency
          desc 0–5 ms, limited only by network RTT
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
